-- title:
--   Tate's inequality dim_k P(𝒪(F[p])) + n ≤ h
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$ with $p$ prime, and let $F$ be an $n$-dimensional formal group law over $k$: an $n$-tuple of power series $F_i$ in the variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,n \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,n$ with vanishing constant terms, linear coefficients $\delta_{ij}$ in each group of variables, and associative substitution; assume $F$ is commutative, i.e. interchanging the two groups of variables leaves each $F_i$ fixed. Let $h$ be a natural number such that the quotient of $k[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ by the ideal generated by the components of $F$'s $p$-th iterated series $[p]_F$ (defined by $[0]_F = 0$ and $[m+1]_F = F([m]_F, X)$) has $k$-dimension $p^h$. Let $L$ be a commutative Hopf algebra over $k$ whose comultiplication is cocommutative, let $\pi : k[[X_1,\dots,X_n]] \to L$ be a surjective $k$-algebra map with kernel exactly that ideal, and let $\Theta : k[[X,Y]] \to L \otimes_k L$ be a $k$-algebra map with $\Theta(G(X)) = \pi G \otimes 1$ and $\Theta(G(Y)) = 1 \otimes \pi G$ for all $G$, such that $\Delta(\pi G) = \Theta(G(F(X,Y)))$ and $\varepsilon(\pi G) = G(0)$ for all $G$. Then the $k$-dimension of the space of primitives of $L$, namely the kernel of $y \mapsto \Delta y - y \otimes 1 - 1 \otimes y$, satisfies $\dim_k P(L) + n \le h$.
--
--   This is the inequality half of Tate's relation $\dim G + \dim G^\vee = \mathrm{height}\,G$, applied to the $p$-torsion $F[p]$ of a commutative formal group of dimension $n$ and height $h$, the hypotheses on $(L,\pi,\Theta)$ saying that $L$ is the coordinate ring of $F[p]$ with the Hopf structure induced by $F$. It feeds the construction of the $\bmod p$ Dieudonné-type realisation, being used in [`MvFormalGroup.exists_add_le_and_forall_exists_sub_sum_smul_mem_span_nthSeries_of_addCoboundary_mem_span`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.exists_add_le_and_forall_exists_sub_sum_smul_mem_span_nthSeries_of_addCoboundary_mem_span).
